WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.310 --> 00:00:04.149
- Hello Believe Nation.

00:00:04.149 --> 00:00:06.874
My name is Evan Carmichael,
my one word is believe

00:00:06.874 --> 00:00:08.949
and I believe that
entrepreneurs will solve

00:00:08.949 --> 00:00:11.150
all the major problems of the world.

00:00:11.150 --> 00:00:13.107
I started the Mentor Me
series on this channel

00:00:13.107 --> 00:00:14.652
with the goal to hang around people

00:00:14.652 --> 00:00:16.017
who've done a lot more than us

00:00:16.017 --> 00:00:18.906
and hopefully by watching
more of their content

00:00:18.906 --> 00:00:20.710
some of their thoughts, their mindsets

00:00:20.710 --> 00:00:22.106
their beliefs, their attitudes

00:00:22.106 --> 00:00:24.373
their way of thinking seeps into us

00:00:24.373 --> 00:00:27.506
to help us become the
best version of ourselves.

00:00:27.506 --> 00:00:29.437
So today we're going to
learn from Maya Angelou

00:00:29.437 --> 00:00:31.967
and some of her most inspiring moments.

00:00:31.967 --> 00:00:33.106
Mentor me Maya.

00:00:33.106 --> 00:00:34.909
Moment number four is my personal favorite

00:00:34.909 --> 00:00:37.058
and I'd love to know which
one you guys like the best.

00:00:37.058 --> 00:00:38.250
Also, as Maya is talking

00:00:38.250 --> 00:00:40.183
if she says something
that really inspires you

00:00:40.183 --> 00:00:41.924
please leave it down
in the comments below.

00:00:41.924 --> 00:00:44.562
Put quotes around it so other
people can be inspired as well

00:00:44.562 --> 00:00:46.588
and when you write it down yourself

00:00:46.588 --> 00:00:48.264
it's much more likely to stick

00:00:48.264 --> 00:00:49.813
so you remember it too.

00:00:49.813 --> 00:00:50.873
Enjoy.

00:00:50.873 --> 00:00:53.706
(inspiring music)

00:01:03.754 --> 00:01:05.509
- I've tried a lot of things.

00:01:05.509 --> 00:01:07.733
I've failed at some things

00:01:07.733 --> 00:01:08.668
and succeeded at some.

00:01:08.668 --> 00:01:10.301
- Yeah but what I love about you

00:01:10.301 --> 00:01:13.745
is that you have, you have attacked it all

00:01:13.745 --> 00:01:14.578
with great passion.

00:01:14.578 --> 00:01:15.828
I mean, look at all the books here

00:01:15.828 --> 00:01:16.741
that you have written.

00:01:16.741 --> 00:01:18.407
I can look at all the things you have done

00:01:18.407 --> 00:01:21.724
from journalist to
poet, to writer to actor

00:01:21.724 --> 00:01:24.272
to producer, all of those kinds of things.

00:01:24.272 --> 00:01:28.439
Which suggest this uncommon
confidence in yourself

00:01:29.334 --> 00:01:31.873
and willingness to risk failure.

00:01:31.873 --> 00:01:32.881
- Yes.

00:01:32.881 --> 00:01:36.714
But maybe it's more
dangerous to risk success.

00:01:37.716 --> 00:01:38.549
- [Charlie] What do you mean?

00:01:38.549 --> 00:01:41.372
- Well a lot of people
don't really want success.

00:01:41.372 --> 00:01:42.324
- [Charlie] I've never understood that.

00:01:42.324 --> 00:01:43.699
- This is true.

00:01:43.699 --> 00:01:45.365
- And maybe because they don't want it

00:01:45.365 --> 00:01:48.556
and the best evidence of
that is that they fail.

00:01:48.556 --> 00:01:50.941
And the best evidence of that
is they don't try things.

00:01:50.941 --> 00:01:51.774
- That's right.

00:01:51.774 --> 00:01:52.607
- [Charlie] Right.

00:01:52.607 --> 00:01:53.440
- That's right.

00:01:53.440 --> 00:01:55.194
But to succeed means that I mean

00:01:55.194 --> 00:01:57.669
you're in front of God

00:01:57.669 --> 00:02:00.557
and lots of responsible people

00:02:00.557 --> 00:02:03.640
and you have to either eat your words

00:02:04.712 --> 00:02:06.129
or stand by them.

00:02:07.066 --> 00:02:11.233
I think that I agreed a
long time ago Charlie Rose

00:02:12.855 --> 00:02:16.022
this may be what my greatest blessing.

00:02:16.914 --> 00:02:20.414
I agreed a long time ago that I would die.

00:02:21.907 --> 00:02:22.740
Now, whew.

00:02:24.439 --> 00:02:26.446
If I can admit that.

00:02:26.446 --> 00:02:29.818
That no matter what happens,
I will do this thing.

00:02:29.818 --> 00:02:32.160
This is the biggest bugaboo of them all.

00:02:32.160 --> 00:02:34.087
I will do that.

00:02:34.087 --> 00:02:37.495
Well then why couldn't I
attempt something lesser?

00:02:37.495 --> 00:02:39.395
- [Charlie] Yeah.

00:02:39.395 --> 00:02:40.695
- So I will try.

00:02:40.695 --> 00:02:42.440
- Well what the '60s

00:02:42.440 --> 00:02:45.107
must have been like for anybody.

00:02:46.292 --> 00:02:49.292
Was it eight or nine assassinations.

00:02:50.893 --> 00:02:53.432
What does that do to a generation?

00:02:53.432 --> 00:02:57.056
Having lived through it and
having known these people.

00:02:57.056 --> 00:02:57.973
This is me.

00:02:59.069 --> 00:03:01.486
I imagine I'd still be angry.

00:03:03.786 --> 00:03:07.810
I'd be angry with my country,
I'd be angry at anybody

00:03:07.810 --> 00:03:11.103
who let that happen to my friends.

00:03:11.103 --> 00:03:12.079
- No.

00:03:12.079 --> 00:03:14.254
If you're not angry

00:03:14.254 --> 00:03:16.004
you're either a stone

00:03:18.904 --> 00:03:21.487
or you're too sick to be angry.

00:03:22.431 --> 00:03:24.549
You should be angry.

00:03:24.549 --> 00:03:25.382
- [Dave] But what do you do?

00:03:25.382 --> 00:03:27.752
- You never mind it,
that's the difference.

00:03:27.752 --> 00:03:29.669
You must not be bitter.

00:03:30.574 --> 00:03:31.407
- [Dave] Oh that's all?

00:03:31.407 --> 00:03:32.240
(laughs)

00:03:32.240 --> 00:03:34.073
- Let me show you why.

00:03:34.981 --> 00:03:37.314
Bitterness is like a cancer.

00:03:38.263 --> 00:03:40.096
It eats upon the host.

00:03:41.343 --> 00:03:44.478
It doesn't do anything to the object

00:03:44.478 --> 00:03:46.240
of its displeasure.

00:03:46.240 --> 00:03:48.627
So you said anger, yes.

00:03:48.627 --> 00:03:51.761
You write it, you paint it, you dance it

00:03:51.761 --> 00:03:53.928
you march it, you vote it.

00:03:54.861 --> 00:03:58.164
You do everything about it, you talk it.

00:03:58.164 --> 00:04:00.069
Never stop talking it.

00:04:00.069 --> 00:04:02.712
When I was seven and a half

00:04:02.712 --> 00:04:03.712
I was raped.

00:04:09.035 --> 00:04:12.952
I won't say severely
raped, all rape is severe.

00:04:18.678 --> 00:04:19.511
The rapist

00:04:22.772 --> 00:04:26.594
was a person very well known to my family.

00:04:26.594 --> 00:04:28.177
I was hospitalized.

00:04:32.944 --> 00:04:35.444
The rapist was let out of jail

00:04:37.308 --> 00:04:39.725
and was found dead that night

00:04:41.063 --> 00:04:42.878
and the police suggested

00:04:42.878 --> 00:04:46.295
that the rapist had been kicked to death.

00:04:47.517 --> 00:04:49.434
I was seven and a half.

00:04:50.620 --> 00:04:52.870
I thought that I had caused

00:04:54.747 --> 00:04:56.210
the man's death

00:04:56.210 --> 00:04:58.710
because I had spoken his name.

00:05:01.437 --> 00:05:05.261
That was my seven and
a half year old logic.

00:05:05.261 --> 00:05:08.261
So I stopped talking for five years.

00:05:11.605 --> 00:05:14.144
Now, to show you again

00:05:14.144 --> 00:05:17.144
how out of evil there can come good.

00:05:19.241 --> 00:05:22.408
In those five years, I read every book

00:05:23.246 --> 00:05:25.579
in the Black School Library.

00:05:27.574 --> 00:05:29.864
I read all the books I could get

00:05:29.864 --> 00:05:33.013
from the White School Library.

00:05:33.013 --> 00:05:35.300
I memorized James Weldon Johnson

00:05:35.300 --> 00:05:39.494
Paul Larnstom, Countee
Cullen and Langston Hughes.

00:05:39.494 --> 00:05:42.577
I memorized Shakespeare, whole plays.

00:05:44.483 --> 00:05:45.400
50 sonnets.

00:05:48.214 --> 00:05:50.759
I memorized Edgar Allen Poe.

00:05:50.759 --> 00:05:52.009
All the poetry.

00:05:53.839 --> 00:05:57.006
Never having heard it, I memorized it.

00:05:58.352 --> 00:06:02.183
I had Longfellow, I had Guy de Maupassant.

00:06:02.183 --> 00:06:03.266
I had Balzac.

00:06:05.400 --> 00:06:06.365
(sighs)

00:06:06.365 --> 00:06:07.991
Rudyard Kipling.

00:06:07.991 --> 00:06:11.083
I mean, it was Catholic kind of reading.

00:06:11.083 --> 00:06:13.500
And Catholic kind of storing.

00:06:15.280 --> 00:06:17.197
When I decided to speak

00:06:18.774 --> 00:06:20.947
I had a lot to say

00:06:20.947 --> 00:06:25.093
and many ways in which
to say what I had to say.

00:06:25.093 --> 00:06:27.996
I listened to the black minister

00:06:27.996 --> 00:06:30.985
and listened to the
melody of the preachers

00:06:30.985 --> 00:06:33.077
and I could tell when they would start up

00:06:33.077 --> 00:06:35.371
on that kind of thing

00:06:35.371 --> 00:06:37.934
whether you know they
mean to take our souls

00:06:37.934 --> 00:06:39.340
straight to heaven

00:06:39.340 --> 00:06:42.992
or whether they meant to
dash us straight to hell.

00:06:42.992 --> 00:06:44.726
I understood it.

00:06:44.726 --> 00:06:46.309
So out of this evil

00:06:47.163 --> 00:06:49.457
which was a dire kind of evil

00:06:49.457 --> 00:06:53.614
because rape on the body of a young person

00:06:53.614 --> 00:06:55.197
more often than not

00:06:56.198 --> 00:06:57.865
introduces cynicism.

00:06:59.172 --> 00:07:01.860
And there's nothing quite so tragic

00:07:01.860 --> 00:07:04.099
as a young cynic.

00:07:04.099 --> 00:07:08.118
Because it means the person
has gone from knowing nothing

00:07:08.118 --> 00:07:10.659
to believing nothing.

00:07:10.659 --> 00:07:14.742
In my case, I was saved
in that muteness you see?

00:07:16.288 --> 00:07:18.705
And the soledad, I was saved.

00:07:19.939 --> 00:07:23.356
And I was able to draw from human thought

00:07:24.673 --> 00:07:28.151
human disappointments and triumphs

00:07:28.151 --> 00:07:30.315
enough to triumph myself.

00:07:30.315 --> 00:07:32.516
- I see you as a brave-heart woman.

00:07:32.516 --> 00:07:33.349
(laughs)

00:07:33.349 --> 00:07:36.325
How do you see yourself Dr. Angelou?

00:07:36.325 --> 00:07:37.825
- A working woman.

00:07:39.086 --> 00:07:40.360
I work hard.

00:07:40.360 --> 00:07:41.193
- [Interviewer] Yes.

00:07:41.193 --> 00:07:42.997
You say, "Always in the process

00:07:42.997 --> 00:07:44.117
"And never take your shoes off."

00:07:44.117 --> 00:07:45.857
- That's it.

00:07:45.857 --> 00:07:47.874
And working all the time.

00:07:47.874 --> 00:07:49.564
I laugh as much as possible.

00:07:49.564 --> 00:07:50.414
- Yeah.

00:07:50.414 --> 00:07:53.334
- I just don't trust
people who don't laugh.

00:07:53.334 --> 00:07:56.219
Who act as if, "I'm serious."

00:07:56.219 --> 00:07:58.302
Who act as if they've got

00:07:59.766 --> 00:08:01.219
some kind of airplane glue

00:08:01.219 --> 00:08:04.832
and stuck their fist to their forehead.

00:08:04.832 --> 00:08:07.249
I think I don't know if
you're serious or not.

00:08:07.249 --> 00:08:08.923
You're boring as the dickens

00:08:08.923 --> 00:08:11.340
but that's for being serious.

00:08:13.499 --> 00:08:14.602
I think if you're serious

00:08:14.602 --> 00:08:17.008
you're trying to make a change.

00:08:17.008 --> 00:08:21.327
If you don't like a situation,
you try to change it.

00:08:21.327 --> 00:08:23.866
Do whatever you can to change it.

00:08:23.866 --> 00:08:26.783
And if everything you do falls flat

00:08:27.787 --> 00:08:29.704
and you can't change it

00:08:32.214 --> 00:08:35.717
then change the way you think about it.

00:08:35.717 --> 00:08:39.281
Move to another position to look at it.

00:08:39.281 --> 00:08:43.364
In doing so, you may find
a new way to change it.

00:08:45.236 --> 00:08:48.793
People will very often
try to respond to you

00:08:48.793 --> 00:08:51.603
on the level on which you address them.

00:08:51.603 --> 00:08:54.235
So if you say, "Aren't you wonderful?

00:08:54.235 --> 00:08:55.107
"Aren't you splendid?

00:08:55.107 --> 00:08:56.910
"My goodness you're beautiful.

00:08:56.910 --> 00:08:58.478
"Oh, you're so bright."

00:08:58.478 --> 00:09:00.705
People will try, even if they're not

00:09:00.705 --> 00:09:04.011
they really will try to
lift themselves up to that.

00:09:04.011 --> 00:09:05.288
On the other hand, if you say

00:09:05.288 --> 00:09:07.298
"You know you're a dog.

00:09:07.298 --> 00:09:09.104
"You really are so low.

00:09:09.104 --> 00:09:11.233
"You'll never be anybody.

00:09:11.233 --> 00:09:12.901
"In fact, you're a nobody now

00:09:12.901 --> 00:09:14.785
"And you never have been."

00:09:14.785 --> 00:09:17.567
Sooner or later, that person will address.

00:09:17.567 --> 00:09:19.769
Will respond on the level

00:09:19.769 --> 00:09:21.814
on which he or she is addressed.

00:09:21.814 --> 00:09:24.647
He will say figuratively or literally

00:09:24.647 --> 00:09:26.808
"Let me show you where dog is.

00:09:26.808 --> 00:09:29.499
"Let me show you where low really is.

00:09:29.499 --> 00:09:30.765
"I will show you that."

00:09:30.765 --> 00:09:33.937
Years ago I did a movie
called Poetic Justice

00:09:33.937 --> 00:09:36.692
and there was a young man the first day

00:09:36.692 --> 00:09:39.619
who cursed so, I couldn't believe it.

00:09:39.619 --> 00:09:41.751
I walked around and behind him.

00:09:41.751 --> 00:09:43.813
Tried to ignore him.

00:09:43.813 --> 00:09:48.584
But the second day, he and
another young man, black man

00:09:48.584 --> 00:09:51.781
ran to each other and
they were about to fight

00:09:51.781 --> 00:09:55.660
and hundreds of extras
started to run away.

00:09:55.660 --> 00:09:59.385
But one black man walked
up to the two young men

00:09:59.385 --> 00:10:01.123
and I walked up

00:10:01.123 --> 00:10:03.664
and I took one by his shoulder.

00:10:03.664 --> 00:10:04.997
I said, "Let me speak to you."

00:10:04.997 --> 00:10:07.347
He said, "If these men
would do, would do."

00:10:07.347 --> 00:10:09.353
I said, "Let me speak to you honey."

00:10:09.353 --> 00:10:10.702
"Well I'll tell you something."

00:10:10.702 --> 00:10:11.989
(grumbles)

00:10:11.989 --> 00:10:14.485
I said, "No let me talk to you please."

00:10:14.485 --> 00:10:17.007
And he finally calmed down.

00:10:17.007 --> 00:10:20.132
And I said, "Do you know
how much you are needed?

00:10:20.132 --> 00:10:22.135
"Do you know what you mean to us?

00:10:22.135 --> 00:10:24.123
"Do you know that hundreds
of years of struggle

00:10:24.123 --> 00:10:26.354
"Have been for you, you?

00:10:26.354 --> 00:10:28.541
"Please baby, take a minute.

00:10:28.541 --> 00:10:30.851
"Don't lose your life on a zoon."

00:10:30.851 --> 00:10:32.490
I put my arm around him.

00:10:32.490 --> 00:10:34.148
He started to weep.

00:10:34.148 --> 00:10:37.347
The tears came down,
that was Tupac Shakur.

00:10:37.347 --> 00:10:41.347
I took him, I walked him
down into a little deli

00:10:42.741 --> 00:10:44.290
and kept his back to the people

00:10:44.290 --> 00:10:46.005
so that they wouldn't see him.

00:10:46.005 --> 00:10:49.495
And I used my hands to dry his cheeks.

00:10:49.495 --> 00:10:53.579
And I kept talking to
him sweetly, sweetly.

00:10:53.579 --> 00:10:57.043
For the next week while I was on that film

00:10:57.043 --> 00:10:59.142
whenever I'd walk by he would be saying

00:10:59.142 --> 00:11:00.715
"So I told him!"

00:11:00.715 --> 00:11:02.542
He said, "Good morning Miss Angelou."

00:11:02.542 --> 00:11:04.550
(laughs)

00:11:04.550 --> 00:11:07.690
Dears, try to introduce courtesy

00:11:07.690 --> 00:11:10.273
into your speech to each other.

00:11:12.131 --> 00:11:13.700
You have no idea what it would do

00:11:13.700 --> 00:11:16.069
for your brother or sister

00:11:16.069 --> 00:11:17.430
to whom you speak.

00:11:17.430 --> 00:11:20.495
And you surely have no idea
what it would do for you.

00:11:20.495 --> 00:11:22.224
It will lift you up.

00:11:22.224 --> 00:11:24.116
At Martin King's request

00:11:24.116 --> 00:11:28.111
I rejoined the Southern
Christian Leadership Conference

00:11:28.111 --> 00:11:30.779
because I had left him to go to Malcolm.

00:11:30.779 --> 00:11:32.712
- Was it really separated,
the movements like that?

00:11:32.712 --> 00:11:34.129
- Oh my goodness.

00:11:35.003 --> 00:11:38.259
The Malcolm was in the
states it was so separated.

00:11:38.259 --> 00:11:42.205
Malcolm even made Martin look like a Tom.

00:11:42.205 --> 00:11:44.982
Until he understood what was happening.

00:11:44.982 --> 00:11:48.937
But that's the wonderful
thing about the icon.

00:11:48.937 --> 00:11:51.151
You continue to grow.

00:11:51.151 --> 00:11:53.393
And you develop courage.

00:11:53.393 --> 00:11:55.683
The most important of all the virtues.

00:11:55.683 --> 00:11:57.827
Because without courage,
you can't practice

00:11:57.827 --> 00:12:01.150
any other virtue consistently.

00:12:01.150 --> 00:12:03.094
If you've seen another truth

00:12:03.094 --> 00:12:07.066
and had enough courage to
change your way of thinking.

00:12:07.066 --> 00:12:09.505
To say hey everybody, you know
what I said in that street?

00:12:09.505 --> 00:12:11.547
I don't believe that anymore.

00:12:11.547 --> 00:12:13.944
A little challenge will straighten me out.

00:12:13.944 --> 00:12:16.629
What I love about my life.

00:12:16.629 --> 00:12:20.360
There's nothing I don't
love about my life.

00:12:20.360 --> 00:12:22.722
It's a struggle, but that's life.

00:12:22.722 --> 00:12:24.210
That's why they call it life.

00:12:24.210 --> 00:12:27.719
When I think cruelty, that's unfair.

00:12:27.719 --> 00:12:28.802
That's nasty.

00:12:30.569 --> 00:12:34.069
Cruelty to anyone, that's rude and stupid.

00:12:36.486 --> 00:12:38.832
But I don't see a lot of that

00:12:38.832 --> 00:12:41.219
and if I do, I try to
do something about it

00:12:41.219 --> 00:12:43.219
rather than I don't just

00:12:45.154 --> 00:12:48.517
sit in the dark and curse the dark.

00:12:48.517 --> 00:12:49.981
I try to light a match.

00:12:49.981 --> 00:12:52.535
You may write me down in history

00:12:52.535 --> 00:12:54.901
with your bitter, twisted lies.

00:12:54.901 --> 00:12:57.379
You may trod me in the very dirt

00:12:57.379 --> 00:12:59.962
but still like dust, I'll rise.

00:13:02.246 --> 00:13:04.487
Does my sassiness upset you?

00:13:04.487 --> 00:13:06.742
Why are you beset with gloom?

00:13:06.742 --> 00:13:10.334
Just because I walk as if I have oil wells

00:13:10.334 --> 00:13:12.433
pumping in my living room.

00:13:12.433 --> 00:13:13.826
(audience laughs)

00:13:13.826 --> 00:13:16.435
Just like moons and like suns

00:13:16.435 --> 00:13:19.471
with the certainty of tides.

00:13:19.471 --> 00:13:22.391
Just like hope springing high.

00:13:22.391 --> 00:13:23.737
Still I rise.

00:13:23.737 --> 00:13:26.179
Did you want to see me broken?

00:13:26.179 --> 00:13:28.726
Bowed head and lowered eyes.

00:13:28.726 --> 00:13:31.876
Shoulders falling down like tear drops.

00:13:31.876 --> 00:13:34.293
Weakened by my soulful cries.

00:13:35.205 --> 00:13:36.882
Does my sassiness upset you?

00:13:36.882 --> 00:13:38.923
(laughs)

00:13:38.923 --> 00:13:42.605
Don't take it so hard just because I laugh

00:13:42.605 --> 00:13:44.794
as if I have gold mines

00:13:44.794 --> 00:13:47.453
digging in my own backyard.

00:13:47.453 --> 00:13:49.628
You can shoot me with your words.

00:13:49.628 --> 00:13:51.866
You can cut me with your lies.

00:13:51.866 --> 00:13:54.057
You can kill me with your hatefulness

00:13:54.057 --> 00:13:56.557
but just like life, I'll rise.

00:13:58.103 --> 00:14:00.770
Does my sexiness offend you, aw.

00:14:01.734 --> 00:14:03.891
(audience laughs)

00:14:03.891 --> 00:14:06.106
Does it come as a surprise

00:14:06.106 --> 00:14:07.106
that I dance

00:14:10.753 --> 00:14:14.700
as if I have diamonds at
the meeting of my thighs.

00:14:14.700 --> 00:14:16.841
(audience laughs)

00:14:16.841 --> 00:14:20.941
Out of the huts of history, shame I rise.

00:14:20.941 --> 00:14:24.852
Up from a past rooted in pain, I rise.

00:14:24.852 --> 00:14:27.993
A black ocean leaping and wide

00:14:27.993 --> 00:14:32.034
welling and swelling
and baring in the tide.

00:14:32.034 --> 00:14:34.379
Leaving behind nights of terror

00:14:34.379 --> 00:14:35.796
and fear, I rise.

00:14:37.187 --> 00:14:40.770
Into a daybreak
miraculously clear, I rise.

00:14:42.429 --> 00:14:45.503
Bringing the gifts that my ancestors gave

00:14:45.503 --> 00:14:47.753
I am the hope and the dream

00:14:48.744 --> 00:14:50.411
of the slave and so.

00:14:52.152 --> 00:14:53.677
(claps)

00:14:53.677 --> 00:14:54.510
Wow!

00:14:55.800 --> 00:14:56.764
There I go.

00:14:56.764 --> 00:14:58.921
(audience applauds)

00:14:58.921 --> 00:15:00.082
- Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:15:00.082 --> 00:15:02.469
I'd love to know what did
you think of this video?

00:15:02.469 --> 00:15:05.298
What was the most inspiring
moment from this video

00:15:05.298 --> 00:15:07.958
that left its mark on you and why.

00:15:07.958 --> 00:15:09.162
Leave it in the comments below.

00:15:09.162 --> 00:15:10.528
I'm super curious to find out.

00:15:10.528 --> 00:15:12.256
I also want to give a
quick shout-out to Lauren.

00:15:12.256 --> 00:15:13.950
Lauren, thank you so much
for picking up a copy

00:15:13.950 --> 00:15:15.578
of my book, Your One Word

00:15:15.578 --> 00:15:18.533
and making that review on
your Youtube channel about it.

00:15:18.533 --> 00:15:20.302
I really, really, really appreciate it

00:15:20.302 --> 00:15:22.181
and I hope that you enjoyed the read.

00:15:22.181 --> 00:15:25.383
- This week I read Your One
Word by Evan Carmichael.

00:15:25.383 --> 00:15:27.666
And I've been a fan of
Evan Carmichael's channel

00:15:27.666 --> 00:15:29.330
here on Youtube for a while.

00:15:29.330 --> 00:15:32.178
He inspires entrepreneurs to go out

00:15:32.178 --> 00:15:33.576
and just do their best.

00:15:33.576 --> 00:15:35.046
- So thank you guys again for watching.

00:15:35.046 --> 00:15:36.046
I believe in you.

00:15:36.046 --> 00:15:38.050
I hope you continue to believe in yourself

00:15:38.050 --> 00:15:40.201
and whatever your one word is.

00:15:40.201 --> 00:15:41.866
Much love.

00:15:41.866 --> 00:15:43.366
I'll see you soon.

